1
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:11,670
A factory packs 1000 screws in every box.

2
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,280
Each screw has a mass of 2.35 grams.

3
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:18,370
What is the mass of all the screws in one box?

4
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,910
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,110
We need 2.35 times 1000.

6
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,690
Watch what happens to the digits.

7
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:32,350
Multiplying by 1000 moves every digit 3 places to the left.

8
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,290
The 2 moves from the ones to the thousands.

9
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:38,440
The answer is 2,350 grams.

10
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:42,300
That is more than 2 kilograms of screws.

11
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,140
Remember place value.

12
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:47,400
In 4.07, the 4 is worth 4 ones.

13
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:52,370
The 0 is worth 0 tenths, and the 7 is worth 7 hundredths.

14
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:59,330
10, 100, 1000 and 10,000 are called powers of 10.

15
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:02,220
We can write them with an index.

16
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:07,010
100 is 10 times 10, so it is 10 to the power 2.

17
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:13,650
1000 is 10 to the power 3, and 10,000 is 10 to the power 4.

18
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:14,920
Notice the pattern.

19
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:18,480
The index is the same as the number of zeros.

20
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:23,330
When you multiply by 10, every digit moves one place to the left.

21
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:26,420
It becomes worth 10 times as much.

22
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:31,850
Multiply by 100, and the digits move 2 places to the left.

23
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:33,990
2.35 becomes 235.

24
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:39,130
Dividing by 10 moves every digit one place to the right.

25
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:41,430
2.35 becomes 0.235.

26
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,530
The decimal point never moves.

27
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,550
Only the digits move.

28
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,360
Your turn.

29
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:49,350
Work out 7.1 times 10 to the power 3.

30
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,920
Pause the video and try it.

31
00:01:52,970 --> 00:01:58,700
10 to the power 3 is 1000, so the digits move 3 places to the left.

32
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:01,120
We fill the gaps with zeros.

33
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,390
The answer is 7,100.

34
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,850
Here is the method.

35
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,160
Step 1: count the zeros, or read the index.

36
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:11,250
10 to the power 3 means 3 places.

37
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,210
Step 2: to multiply, move the digits left.

38
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:17,100
To divide, move the digits right.

39
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:20,160
Step 3: fill any gaps with zeros.

40
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:21,160
Step 4: check.

41
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:23,750
Multiplying makes the number bigger.

42
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,170
Dividing makes it smaller.

43
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:29,830
Work out 56 divided by 1000.

44
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:35,460
1000 has 3 zeros, so the digits move 3 places to the right.

45
00:02:35,510 --> 00:02:40,650
56 becomes 5.6, then 0.56, then 0.056.

46
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:43,480
A zero fills the empty tenths place.

47
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,610
The answer is 0.056.

48
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:46,410
Your turn.

49
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:49,720
Work out 85 divided by 10 to the power 4.

50
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:52,900
Pause and work it out.

51
00:02:52,950 --> 00:02:55,840
10 to the power 4 is 10,000.

52
00:02:55,890 --> 00:02:59,830
Move the digits 4 places to the right.

53
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:02,270
85 becomes 0.0085.

54
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,490
Fill the gap.

55
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:06,960
9.2 times something equals 920.

56
00:03:07,010 --> 00:03:10,200
The 9 has moved from the ones to the hundreds.

57
00:03:10,250 --> 00:03:12,790
That is 2 places to the left.

58
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:17,700
2 places means 10 to the power 2, which is 100.

59
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:20,950
A sheet of paper is 0.09 millimetres thick.

60
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,360
How thick is a pile of 1000 sheets, in centimetres?

61
00:03:25,410 --> 00:03:29,910
0.09 times 1000: move the digits 3 places left.

62
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,690
That is 90 millimetres.

63
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,960
There are 10 millimetres in a centimetre.

64
00:03:36,010 --> 00:03:37,720
90 divided by 10 is 9.

65
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:40,820
The pile is 9 centimetres thick.

66
00:03:40,870 --> 00:03:43,110
Noor works out 6.8 times 10.

67
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:45,950
Which line goes wrong first?

68
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,200
Line 1 is wrong.

69
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:50,560
Adding a zero only works for whole numbers.

70
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:54,860
6.80 is the same as 6.8, so nothing has changed.

71
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:58,550
The digits must move one place to the left.

72
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,730
6.8 times 10 is 68.

73
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:05,050
Powers of 10 are built into the metric system.

74
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:06,550
Kilo means 1000.

75
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:12,740
So 1 kilometre is 1000 metres, and 1 kilogram is 1000 grams.

76
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:18,880
A 5 kilometre run is 5 times 1000, which is 5000 metres.

77
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:21,590
Milli means divide by 1000.

78
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:29,890
A 250 millilitre glass of juice is 250 divided by 1000, which is 0.25 litres.

79
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:31,200
One last question.

80
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:33,680
Which calculation is equal to 0.6?

81
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:37,050
Pause the video and choose.

82
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,800
60 divided by 100.

83
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:42,500
The digits move 2 places to the right.

84
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:45,970
60 becomes 0.60, which is 0.6.

85
00:04:46,020 --> 00:04:51,560
To remember: the index of a power of 10 tells you the number of zeros.

86
00:04:51,610 --> 00:04:53,640
To multiply, digits move left.

87
00:04:53,690 --> 00:04:56,200
To divide, digits move right.

88
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,670
Fill gaps with zeros.

89
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,450
The decimal point does not move.

90
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:05,550
And check: multiplying makes it bigger, dividing makes it smaller.

91
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:10,670
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.1 on Camday.
